lesson: 196
title: Before and after: giving to make equal
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: When one child gives things to another, the total stays the same. If they then have the same number, each has half of the total.
explain: Before the gift, the giver had the gift more than that half; the other had the gift less.
explain: Tom and Ann have 40 marbles. After Tom gives Ann 5, they have the same: 40 ÷ 2 = 20 each, so Tom had 20 + 5 = 25 at first.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing e=6..40 g=2..15
need: e - g >= 2
let: T = 2 * e
let: B = e - g
answer: e + g
exercise: {a} and {b} have {T} {t} together. After {a} gives {b} {g} {t}, they have the same number. How many {t} did {a} have at first?
exercise: Together {a} and {b} have {T} {t}. If {a} gives {g} of {a.his} {t} to {b}, the two will have equally many. How many {t} does {a} have?
exercise: Two shelves hold {T} books. When {g} books are moved from the top shelf to the bottom shelf, both shelves hold the same number. How many books were on the top shelf at first?
exercise: After {a} gives {g} {t} to {b}, each of them has {e} {t}. How many {t} did {a} have before?
exercise: {b} has {B} {t}. After {a} gives {b} {g} {t}, they have equally many. How many {t} did {a} have at the start?
exercise: Two baskets hold {T} apples. After {g} apples are taken from the first basket and put into the second, the baskets hold the same number. How many apples were in the first basket?
test: The two classes have {T} pupils between them. If {g} pupils moved from the first class to the second, the classes would be equal. How many pupils are in the first class?
test: {a} has {2 * g} more {t} than {b}, and together they have {T}. How many {t} does {a} have?
test: {b} owns {B} {t}. {a} would have to hand over {g} of {a.his} own {t} for them both to have the same amount. How many {t} does {a} own?
test: Two tanks hold {T} litres of water in all. Pouring {g} litres from the first tank into the second leaves equal amounts in them. How many litres were in the first tank?
exercise: {a} and {b} have {T} {t} in total. When {a} gives {g} {t} to {b}, they have equal numbers. How many {t} did {a} start with?
exercise: How many {t} did {a} have at first, if {a} and {b} had {T} {t} altogether and after {a} gave {b} {g} of them they had the same number?
exercise: Two classrooms in a school in Ohio have {T} chairs in all. Moving {g} chairs from the first room to the second makes the rooms equal. How many chairs were in the first room at first?
exercise: {T} {t} together; {a} gives {b} {g}, and then they have the same. How many did {a} have at first?
exercise: {a} has some {t} and {b} has {B}. Once {a} hands {b} {g} {t}, both have the same number. How many {t} did {a} have to begin with?
exercise: Two buses in Toronto carry {T} passengers. When {g} passengers move from the first bus to the second, both buses carry the same number. How many passengers were on the first bus before?
exercise: {a} gives away {g} {t} to {b}, and then each of them has {e.words} {t}. How many {t} did {a} have before giving?
exercise: Two piggy banks in Sydney hold {T} coins. After {g} coins are moved from the first piggy bank to the second, they hold the same number of coins. How many coins were in the first piggy bank?
test: If {g} sheep crossed from the first field to the second, the two fields of a farm in Wales would hold the same number. Together they hold {T} sheep. How many sheep are in the first field?
test: {a} owns {2 * g} {t} more than {b}. Combined, they own {T}. How many {t} are {a}'s?
test: {b} has {B} {t}. If {a} handed {g} {t} over to {b}, both would own the same number. How many {t} does {a} own now?
test: How many {t} did {a} start with, if after passing {g} of them to {b} each child had half of their {T} {t}?
test: In a library in Auckland, two carts hold {T} books. Shifting {g} books from the first cart to the second leaves the carts with equal numbers. How many books did the first cart hold at first?
test: {a} and {b} share {T} {t} unevenly. To even things up, {a} donates {g} {t} to {b}. How many {t} did {a} have before that?
